<!--
  ICS Watch Dog - OT Enhanced Sysmon Configuration
  Version:      v2.1
  Author:       ICS Watch Dog Project (https://icswatchdog.com)
  Project:      https://github.com/cutaway-security/ICSWatchDog
  License:      Creative Commons Attribution 4.0

  Minimum Sysmon:   v13+ (schema 4.50)
  Target:           ICS/OT Windows systems with established monitoring programs

  SANS ICS 5 Critical Controls Supported:
    #1 ICS Incident Response - Forensic evidence via process, file, registry, network logs
    #2 Defensible Architecture - Detection of processes crossing network boundaries
    #3 ICS Network Visibility - ENHANCED: industrial protocol port monitoring identifies
        which processes communicate on Modbus, EtherNet/IP, OPC-UA, DNP3, S7comm, BACnet,
        and other industrial ports (SANS Control #3 primary focus of this config)
    #4 Secure Remote Access - Detection of known remote access / RMM tools
    #5 Vulnerability Management - Software execution, driver loading, service change logging

  CIS Benchmark Alignment:
    Complements CIS Microsoft Windows 10/11 Enterprise Benchmark
    Extends Section 17 (Advanced Audit Policy) with process-level telemetry
    NOTE: Sysmon monitors process-to-port connections, NOT protocol payloads.
    For protocol-level inspection, use dedicated ICS network monitoring tools.

  MITRE ATT&CK Coverage:
    T0830     - Adversary-in-the-Middle (ICS) - industrial protocol monitoring
    T0855     - Unauthorized Command Message (ICS) - industrial protocol monitoring
    T0857     - Modify Controller Tasking (ICS) - firmware files
    T1003.001 - LSASS Memory
    T1486     - Data Encrypted for Impact (ransom note detection, EKANS)
    T1490     - Inhibit System Recovery
    T1547.001 - Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder
    T1559.001 - Component Object Model (DCOM/OPC registry)
    T1562.001 - Disable or Modify Tools
    T1562.004 - Disable or Modify System Firewall
    T1565.001 - Stored Data Manipulation (ICS project files)
    T1565.002 - Transmitted Data Manipulation (ICS vendor directories)
    T1572     - Protocol Tunneling

  DESCRIPTION:
    This is the OT ENHANCED configuration. It builds on the OT Baseline
    (sysmonconfig-baseline-ot.xml) with the following additions:

    - INDUSTRIAL PORT MONITORING: NetworkConnect include rules that log which
      processes communicate on industrial protocol ports. This is the primary
      addition over the OT Baseline. If an unexpected process connects to
      Modbus/TCP port 502, this config will log it with full process context.

    - EXPANDED VENDOR SOFTWARE MONITORING: Additional OT vendor process names
      and installation paths beyond the baseline examples.

    - BROADER FILE MONITORING: Additional ICS-relevant file types and OT
      software configuration file monitoring.

    - EXPANDED REGISTRY MONITORING: OPC and DCOM configuration keys relevant
      to OT communication infrastructure.

    All include rules use the ATT&CK structured tagging convention.
    See https://icswatchdog.com/attack-tagging/ for the full specification.

    Industrial protocols monitored (via NetworkConnect port rules):
      Modbus TCP (502), EtherNet/IP (44818, 2222), OPC-UA (4840),
      OPC DA/DCOM (135 RPC), DNP3 (20000), S7comm (102),
      BACnet/IP (47808), IEC 61850 MMS (102), IEC 60870-5-104 (2404),
      MQTT (1883, 8883), Ignition Gateway (8088, 8043)

    VENDOR SOFTWARE EXAMPLES: The vendor process rules are EXAMPLES. They MUST
    be validated against your actual installations.

  TUNING:
    Administrators MUST review and tune this configuration for their environment.
    - Validate vendor process names and paths against your actual installations
    - Add your site-specific ICS/OT software following the examples provided
    - Review industrial port rules and add ports specific to your environment
    - Review remote access tool rules and exclude sanctioned tools
    - Test in a non-production environment before deploying to production systems
    - Consider system performance impact (see icswatchdog.com/deployment/)

  DISCLAIMER:
    This configuration is provided as-is for educational and operational use.
    It is NOT tested against all environments and may require tuning for your
    specific systems. Cutaway Security, LLC and contributors assume no liability
    for any impact resulting from the use of this configuration. Users are
    responsible for testing in their own environments before production deployment.
    This is especially critical in ICS/OT environments where system availability
    and safety are paramount.

  REFERENCES:
    - SANS ICS 5 Critical Controls: https://www.sans.org/white-papers/five-ics-cybersecurity-critical-controls
    - CISA RMM Guidance: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-025a
    - LOLRMM Project: https://lolrmm.io/
    - Microsoft Sysmon: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/sysmon
    - CIS Benchmarks: https://www.cisecurity.org/benchmark/microsoft_windows_desktop
    - CISA Ransomware Guide: https://www.cisa.gov/stopransomware/ransomware-guide
-->

<Sysmon schemaversion="4.50">
  <HashAlgorithms>md5,sha256,IMPHASH</HashAlgorithms>
  <!-- CheckRevocation: checks loaded driver code-signing certificate revocation status.
       Requires network access to CRL distribution points / OCSP responders.
       Disabled by default for OT configs because many OT systems are air-gapped or
       have restricted network access. Set to True if this system can reach CRL endpoints. -->
  <CheckRevocation>False</CheckRevocation>

  <EventFiltering>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 1: PROCESS CREATION [ProcessCreate]
    Same as OT Baseline.
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="ProcessCreate" groupRelation="or">
      <ProcessCreate onmatch="exclude">
        <Image name="exclude=Background Task Host" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\backgroundTaskHost.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Runtime Broker" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\RuntimeBroker.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Search Protocol Host" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\SearchProtocolHost.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Search Filter Host" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\SearchFilterHost.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Audio Device Graph" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\audiodg.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=conhost system noise" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\conhost.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Microsoft Update Notification" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\musNotification.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Microsoft Update Notification UX" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\musNotificationUx.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Error Reporting" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\WerFault.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Error Reporting (32-bit)" condition="is">C:\Windows\SysWOW64\WerFault.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Error Reporting manager" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\wermgr.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Software Protection Platform" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\SppExtComObj.Exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Compatibility Telemetry" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\CompatTelRunner.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Defender MsMpEng" condition="is">C:\Program Files\Windows Defender\MsMpEng.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Defender NisSrv" condition="is">C:\Program Files\Windows Defender\NisSrv.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Defender MpCmdRun" condition="is">C:\Program Files\Windows Defender\MpCmdRun.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Defender Platform MsMpEng" condition="is">C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Windows Defender\Platform\MsMpEng.exe</Image>
      </ProcessCreate>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
      T1490 Inhibit System Recovery + T1562.001 Disable or Modify Tools
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="ProcessCreate-RansomwareIndicators" groupRelation="or">
      <ProcessCreate onmatch="include">
        <CommandLine name="technique_id=T1490,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Ransomware shadow copy deletion via vssadmin" condition="contains">delete shadows</CommandLine>
        <CommandLine name="technique_id=T1490,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Ransomware shadow copy deletion via WMI" condition="contains">shadowcopy delete</CommandLine>
        <CommandLine name="technique_id=T1490,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Ransomware Windows recovery disabled via bcdedit" condition="contains">recoveryenabled no</CommandLine>
        <CommandLine name="technique_id=T1490,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Ransomware boot status policy bypass via bcdedit" condition="contains">bootstatuspolicy ignoreallfailures</CommandLine>
        <CommandLine name="technique_id=T1490,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Ransomware Windows backup catalog deletion via wbadmin" condition="contains">delete catalog</CommandLine>
        <CommandLine name="technique_id=T1490,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Ransomware safe mode boot configuration" condition="contains">bcdedit /set safeboot</CommandLine>
        <CommandLine name="technique_id=T1562.001,technique=Disable or Modify Tools,detection=Ransomware Defender realtime monitoring disabled" condition="contains">DisableRealtimeMonitoring $true</CommandLine>
        <CommandLine name="technique_id=T1562.001,technique=Disable or Modify Tools,detection=Ransomware Defender path exclusion added" condition="contains">ExclusionPath</CommandLine>
      </ProcessCreate>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 2: FILE CREATION TIME CHANGED [FileCreateTime]
    MITRE ATT&CK: T1070.006 (Timestomp)
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="FileCreateTime" groupRelation="or">
      <FileCreateTime onmatch="exclude">
        <Image name="exclude=svchost timestamp updates" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\svchost.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=msiexec install timestamp updates" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\msiexec.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Chrome browser timestamp updates" condition="end with">\Chrome\Application\chrome.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Edge browser timestamp updates" condition="end with">\Microsoft\Edge\Application\msedge.exe</Image>
      </FileCreateTime>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 3: NETWORK CONNECTION [NetworkConnect]
    ENHANCED: Two RuleGroups for NetworkConnect.
    RuleGroup 1: general exclude (same as OT Baseline).
    RuleGroup 2: INDUSTRIAL PROTOCOL PORT MONITORING (primary enhancement).
    NOTE: Sysmon monitors WHICH PROCESS connects to WHICH PORT. It does NOT
    inspect protocol payloads. For protocol-level monitoring, use dedicated
    ICS network monitoring tools (e.g., Zeek, Claroty, Nozomi, Dragos).
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="NetworkConnect-General" groupRelation="or">
      <NetworkConnect onmatch="exclude">
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Defender MsMpEng network" condition="is">C:\Program Files\Windows Defender\MsMpEng.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Windows Defender Platform MsMpEng network" condition="is">C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Windows Defender\Platform\MsMpEng.exe</Image>
      </NetworkConnect>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
      T0830 Adversary-in-the-Middle (ICS) + T0855 Unauthorized Command Message (ICS)
      Industrial protocol port monitoring. SANS ICS 5 Critical Control #3 primary focus.
      These rules log connections on known industrial protocol ports with descriptive
      RuleNames for SIEM correlation. An unexpected process connecting to Modbus TCP
      port 502 may indicate reconnaissance, lateral movement, or unauthorized commands.
      IMPORTANT: These are DEFAULT ports. Your environment may use non-standard ports.
      Add your site-specific ports following the same pattern.
      References:
        https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0830/
        https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0855/
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="NetworkConnect-IndustrialPorts" groupRelation="or">
      <NetworkConnect onmatch="include">
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to Modbus TCP port 502" condition="is">502</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to EtherNet/IP TCP port 44818" condition="is">44818</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to EtherNet/IP implicit messaging port 2222" condition="is">2222</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to OPC-UA port 4840" condition="is">4840</DestinationPort>
        <!-- NOTE: Port 135 (RPC) is also used by many Windows services. On an OT
             system, unexpected RPC connections warrant review. -->
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to OPC DA/DCOM RPC port 135" condition="is">135</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to DNP3 port 20000" condition="is">20000</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to S7comm/ISO-TSAP port 102" condition="is">102</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to BACnet/IP port 47808" condition="is">47808</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to IEC 60870-5-104 port 2404" condition="is">2404</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to MQTT port 1883" condition="is">1883</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830|T0855,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to MQTT over TLS port 8883" condition="is">8883</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to Ignition Gateway HTTP port 8088" condition="is">8088</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to Ignition Gateway HTTPS port 8043" condition="is">8043</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to OSIsoft PI Data Archive port 5450" condition="is">5450</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to GE SRTP port 18245" condition="is">18245</DestinationPort>
        <!-- NOTE: PROFINET DCP uses UDP broadcast, not typically TCP connections.
             PROFINET RT/IRT operates at Layer 2 (not visible to Sysmon).
             Port 34962-34964 used for PROFINET IO context management. -->
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to PROFINET IO CM port 34962" condition="is">34962</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to PROFINET IO alarm port 34963" condition="is">34963</DestinationPort>
        <DestinationPort name="technique_id=T0830,technique=Adversary-in-the-Middle,detection=Process connecting to PROFINET IO data port 34964" condition="is">34964</DestinationPort>
      </NetworkConnect>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 5: PROCESS TERMINATED [ProcessTerminate]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="ProcessTerminate" groupRelation="or">
      <ProcessTerminate onmatch="exclude">
        <Image name="exclude=Background Task Host termination" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\backgroundTaskHost.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=Runtime Broker termination" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\RuntimeBroker.exe</Image>
        <Image name="exclude=conhost termination noise" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\conhost.exe</Image>
      </ProcessTerminate>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 6: DRIVER LOADED [DriverLoad]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="DriverLoad" groupRelation="or">
      <DriverLoad onmatch="exclude">
        <Signature name="exclude=Microsoft signed driver" condition="contains">Microsoft</Signature>
        <Signature name="exclude=Windows signed driver" condition="contains">Windows</Signature>
      </DriverLoad>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 7: IMAGE LOADED [ImageLoad]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="ImageLoad" groupRelation="or">
      <ImageLoad onmatch="include"/>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 8: CREATE REMOTE THREAD [CreateRemoteThread]
    MITRE ATT&CK: T1055 (Process Injection)
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="CreateRemoteThread" groupRelation="or">
      <CreateRemoteThread onmatch="exclude">
        <SourceImage name="exclude=csrss legitimate remote thread" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\csrss.exe</SourceImage>
        <SourceImage name="exclude=wininit legitimate remote thread" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\wininit.exe</SourceImage>
        <SourceImage name="exclude=winlogon legitimate remote thread" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\winlogon.exe</SourceImage>
        <SourceImage name="exclude=services legitimate remote thread" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\services.exe</SourceImage>
        <SourceImage name="exclude=lsass legitimate remote thread" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\lsass.exe</SourceImage>
        <SourceImage name="exclude=svchost legitimate remote thread" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\svchost.exe</SourceImage>
      </CreateRemoteThread>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 9: RAW ACCESS READ [RawAccessRead]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="RawAccessRead" groupRelation="or">
      <RawAccessRead onmatch="include"/>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
      T1003.001 LSASS Memory
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="ProcessAccess" groupRelation="or">
      <ProcessAccess onmatch="include">
        <TargetImage name="technique_id=T1003.001,technique=LSASS Memory,detection=Process accessing lsass.exe" condition="is">C:\Windows\System32\lsass.exe</TargetImage>
      </ProcessAccess>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 11: FILE CREATED [FileCreate]
    ENHANCED: Builds on OT Baseline with additional ICS file types,
    expanded vendor directory monitoring, and OT configuration files.
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="FileCreate" groupRelation="or">
      <FileCreate onmatch="include">
        <!-- Persistence locations -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1547.001,technique=Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder,detection=File created in Start Menu" condition="contains">\Start Menu</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1547.001,technique=Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder,detection=File created in Startup folder" condition="contains">\Startup</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1053.005,technique=Scheduled Task,detection=Scheduled task XML created in Tasks directory" condition="contains">\Windows\System32\Tasks</TargetFilename>
        <!-- Executable and script file types -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1204.002,technique=Malicious File,detection=Executable file created" condition="end with">.exe</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1574.002,technique=DLL Side-Loading,detection=DLL file created" condition="end with">.dll</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1543.003|T1014,technique=Windows Service,detection=System driver (.sys) file created" condition="end with">.sys</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1059.003,technique=Windows Command Shell,detection=Batch script created" condition="end with">.bat</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1059.003,technique=Windows Command Shell,detection=Command script created" condition="end with">.cmd</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1059.001,technique=PowerShell,detection=PowerShell script created" condition="end with">.ps1</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1059.005,technique=Visual Basic,detection=VBScript file created" condition="end with">.vbs</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1059.007,technique=JavaScript,detection=JavaScript file created" condition="end with">.js</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1059.005,technique=Visual Basic,detection=Windows Script File created" condition="end with">.wsf</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1218.005,technique=Mshta,detection=HTML Application file created" condition="end with">.hta</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1546.002,technique=Screensaver,detection=Screensaver executable created" condition="end with">.scr</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1218.007,technique=Msiexec,detection=MSI installer file created" condition="end with">.msi</TargetFilename>
        <!-- User/temp locations -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1105,technique=Ingress Tool Transfer,detection=File created in user Downloads folder" condition="contains">\Downloads\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1105,technique=Ingress Tool Transfer,detection=File created in user AppData Temp folder" condition="contains">\AppData\Local\Temp\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1105,technique=Ingress Tool Transfer,detection=File created in ProgramData folder" condition="contains">\ProgramData\</TargetFilename>

        <!--
          T1565.001 Stored Data Manipulation (ICS project files)
          PLC programming and HMI/SCADA project files.
        -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Siemens TIA Portal project file (.ap17) created" condition="end with">.ap17</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Siemens TIA Portal project file (.ap18) created" condition="end with">.ap18</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Siemens TIA Portal project file (.ap19) created" condition="end with">.ap19</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Siemens STEP 7 project file created" condition="end with">.s7p</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=CODESYS project file created" condition="end with">.project</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=IEC 61131 structured text source created" condition="end with">.st</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=AVEVA InTouch application file created" condition="end with">.app</TargetFilename>

        <!--
          T0857 Modify Controller Tasking + T1601 System Firmware (ICS ATT&CK)
          Firmware files.
        -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T0857|T1601,technique=Modify Controller Tasking,detection=Firmware HEX file created" condition="end with">.hex</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T0857|T1601,technique=Modify Controller Tasking,detection=Firmware binary file created" condition="end with">.bin</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T0857|T1601,technique=Modify Controller Tasking,detection=Firmware update file created" condition="end with">.fw</TargetFilename>

        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=OPC configuration file created" condition="end with">.opf</TargetFilename>

        <!-- Archives -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1560.001,technique=Archive via Utility,detection=ZIP archive created" condition="end with">.zip</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1560.001,technique=Archive via Utility,detection=RAR archive created" condition="end with">.rar</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1560.001,technique=Archive via Utility,detection=7z archive created" condition="end with">.7z</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1204.002|T1027.006,technique=Malicious File,detection=ISO file created (common malware container)" condition="end with">.iso</TargetFilename>

        <!--
          T1565.001 Stored Data Manipulation
          ENHANCED: Additional ICS vendor project file formats.
        -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Rockwell Studio 5000 project (.ACD) created" condition="end with">.ACD</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Rockwell RSLogix project (.RSS) created" condition="end with">.RSS</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Rockwell RSLogix 5000 project (.L5K) created" condition="end with">.L5K</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Rockwell RSLogix 5000 export (.L5X) created" condition="end with">.L5X</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Schneider Unity Pro project (.stu) created" condition="end with">.stu</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=Schneider EcoStruxure project (.xef) created" condition="end with">.xef</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T0836|T1565.001,technique=Modify Parameter,detection=SEL relay settings file created" condition="end with">.rdb</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T0852,technique=Screen Capture,detection=SEL relay event report created" condition="end with">.cev</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.001,technique=Stored Data Manipulation,detection=GE Proficy project file created" condition="end with">.cmp</TargetFilename>
        <!--
          T1552.004 Private Keys + T1556 Modify Authentication Process
          OPC UA certificate changes may indicate tampering with OT authentication.
        -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1552.004|T1556,technique=Private Keys,detection=OPC UA certificate (.der) created" condition="end with">.der</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1552.004|T1556,technique=Private Keys,detection=OPC UA certificate (.pem) created" condition="end with">.pem</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1005,technique=Data from Local System,detection=ICS configuration CSV export created" condition="end with">.csv</TargetFilename>

        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.001,technique=Hidden Files and Directories,detection=File staged in Recycle Bin" condition="contains">\$Recycle.Bin\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1484.001,technique=Group Policy Modification,detection=Group Policy file modified" condition="contains">\GroupPolicy\</TargetFilename>

        <!-- Ransom note detection -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1486,technique=Data Encrypted for Impact,detection=Ransom note filename containing DECRYPT" condition="contains">DECRYPT</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1486,technique=Data Encrypted for Impact,detection=Ransom note filename containing RANSOM" condition="contains">RANSOM</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1486,technique=Data Encrypted for Impact,detection=Ransom note filename containing RECOVER" condition="contains">RECOVER</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1486,technique=Data Encrypted for Impact,detection=EKANS ransomware note (Decrypt-Your-Files.txt)" condition="end with">Decrypt-Your-Files.txt</TargetFilename>

        <!--
          T1565.002 Transmitted Data Manipulation
          ICS vendor installation directories.
        -->
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Siemens installation directory" condition="contains">\Siemens\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Rockwell Software directory" condition="contains">\Rockwell Software\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in FactoryTalk directory" condition="contains">\FactoryTalk\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Schneider Electric directory" condition="contains">\Schneider Electric\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Wonderware directory" condition="contains">\Wonderware\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in ArchestrA directory" condition="contains">\ArchestrA\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in OSIsoft PI directory" condition="contains">\PIPC\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Inductive Automation Ignition directory" condition="contains">\Inductive Automation\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Kepware directory" condition="contains">\Kepware\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in SEL directory" condition="contains">\SEL\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in CODESYS directory" condition="contains">\CODESYS\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in GE Digital directory" condition="contains">\GE Digital\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in GE iFIX directory" condition="contains">\GE\iFIX\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Honeywell directory" condition="contains">\Honeywell\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Emerson directory" condition="contains">\Emerson\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in ABB directory" condition="contains">\ABB\</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1565.002,technique=Transmitted Data Manipulation,detection=File created in Yokogawa directory" condition="contains">\Yokogawa\</TargetFilename>
      </FileCreate>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 12, 13, 14: REGISTRY EVENTS [RegistryEvent]
    ENHANCED: Builds on OT Baseline with OPC/DCOM registry monitoring.
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="RegistryEvent" groupRelation="or">
      <RegistryEvent onmatch="include">
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1547.001,technique=Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder,detection=Registry Run key modified" condition="contains">\CurrentVersion\Run</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1547.001,technique=Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder,detection=Registry RunOnce key modified" condition="contains">\CurrentVersion\RunOnce</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1547.001,technique=Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder,detection=RunServices key modified" condition="contains">\CurrentVersion\RunServices</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1547.001,technique=Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder,detection=Explorer Policies Run key modified" condition="contains">\CurrentVersion\Policies\Explorer\Run</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1543.003,technique=Windows Service,detection=Windows service registry key modified" condition="contains">\CurrentControlSet\Services</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1053.005,technique=Scheduled Task,detection=Scheduled task cache modified" condition="contains">\Schedule\TaskCache</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1546.010,technique=AppInit DLLs,detection=AppInit_DLLs registry value modified" condition="contains">\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Windows\AppInit_DLLs</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1546.012,technique=Image File Execution Options Injection,detection=IFEO registry key modified" condition="contains">\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1547.004,technique=Winlogon Helper DLL,detection=Winlogon Shell value modified" condition="contains">\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon\Shell</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1547.004,technique=Winlogon Helper DLL,detection=Winlogon Userinit value modified" condition="contains">\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon\Userinit</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1562.001,technique=Disable or Modify Tools,detection=AppLocker policy modified" condition="contains">\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\SrpV2</TargetObject>
        <!--
          T1559.001 Component Object Model + T1562.004 Disable or Modify System Firewall
          ENHANCED: OPC/DCOM config changes can affect or compromise OT communications.
          Firewall rule changes may expose industrial ports.
        -->
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1559.001,technique=Component Object Model,detection=DCOM Ole configuration modified" condition="contains">\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Ole</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1559.001,technique=Component Object Model,detection=OPC server registration modified" condition="contains">\OPC\</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1562.004,technique=Disable or Modify System Firewall,detection=Windows Firewall rules modified" condition="contains">\Services\SharedAccess\Parameters\FirewallPolicy</TargetObject>
        <!-- Ransomware-relevant registry changes -->
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1490,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=SafeBoot configuration modified" condition="contains">\Control\SafeBoot</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1112|T1003.001,technique=Modify Registry,detection=WDigest credential caching enabled" condition="contains">\SecurityProviders\WDigest</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1562.001,technique=Disable or Modify Tools,detection=Windows Defender policy modified" condition="contains">\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender</TargetObject>
        <TargetObject name="technique_id=T1562.001,technique=Disable or Modify Tools,detection=Sysmon Autologger registry tampering" condition="contains">\Autologger\EventLog-Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon</TargetObject>
      </RegistryEvent>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 15: FILE CREATE STREAM HASH [FileCreateStreamHash]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="FileCreateStreamHash" groupRelation="or">
      <FileCreateStreamHash onmatch="include">
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.004|T1553.005,technique=NTFS File Attributes,detection=Executable Mark of the Web stream created" condition="end with">.exe</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.004|T1553.005,technique=NTFS File Attributes,detection=DLL Mark of the Web stream created" condition="end with">.dll</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.004|T1553.005,technique=NTFS File Attributes,detection=Batch script Mark of the Web stream created" condition="end with">.bat</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.004|T1553.005,technique=NTFS File Attributes,detection=Command script Mark of the Web stream created" condition="end with">.cmd</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.004|T1553.005,technique=NTFS File Attributes,detection=PowerShell script Mark of the Web stream created" condition="end with">.ps1</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.004|T1553.005,technique=NTFS File Attributes,detection=VBScript Mark of the Web stream created" condition="end with">.vbs</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.004|T1553.005,technique=NTFS File Attributes,detection=JavaScript Mark of the Web stream created" condition="end with">.js</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1564.004|T1553.005,technique=NTFS File Attributes,detection=HTA Mark of the Web stream created" condition="end with">.hta</TargetFilename>
      </FileCreateStreamHash>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 17, 18: NAMED PIPE EVENTS [PipeEvent]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="PipeCreated" groupRelation="or">
      <PipeEvent onmatch="exclude">
        <PipeName name="exclude=lsass system pipe" condition="is">\lsass</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="exclude=Workstation service pipe" condition="is">\wkssvc</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="exclude=Server service pipe" condition="is">\srvsvc</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="exclude=Remote registry pipe" condition="is">\winreg</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="exclude=Print spooler pipe" condition="is">\spoolss</PipeName>
      </PipeEvent>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
      T1572 Protocol Tunneling + T1021.002 SMB Admin Shares + T1003.001 LSASS Memory
      C2 framework named pipes and lateral movement tool indicators.
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="PipeCreated-C2Detection" groupRelation="or">
      <PipeEvent onmatch="include">
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1572|T1071,technique=Protocol Tunneling,detection=Cobalt Strike default named pipe MSSE-" condition="begin with">\MSSE-</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1572|T1071,technique=Protocol Tunneling,detection=Cobalt Strike post-exploitation pipe postex_" condition="begin with">\postex_</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1572|T1071,technique=Protocol Tunneling,detection=Cobalt Strike status pipe" condition="begin with">\status_</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1572|T1071,technique=Protocol Tunneling,detection=Cobalt Strike msagent pipe" condition="begin with">\msagent_</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1021.002|T1570,technique=SMB Admin Shares,detection=PsExec service pipe PSEXESVC" condition="is">\PSEXESVC</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1021.002|T1570,technique=SMB Admin Shares,detection=PAExec lateral movement pipe" condition="begin with">\paexec</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1021.002|T1570,technique=SMB Admin Shares,detection=RemCom lateral movement pipe" condition="begin with">\remcom</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1021.002|T1570,technique=SMB Admin Shares,detection=CSExec lateral movement pipe" condition="begin with">\csexec</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1003.001,technique=LSASS Memory,detection=Mimikatz lsadump named pipe" condition="is">\lsadump</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1003.005,technique=Cached Domain Credentials,detection=Cachedump named pipe" condition="is">\cachedump</PipeName>
        <PipeName name="technique_id=T1003.001,technique=LSASS Memory,detection=Windows Credential Editor service pipe" condition="is">\wceservicepipe</PipeName>
      </PipeEvent>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 19, 20, 21: WMI EVENTS [WmiEvent]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="WmiEvent" groupRelation="or">
      <WmiEvent onmatch="exclude"/>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 22: DNS QUERY [DnsQuery]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="DnsQuery" groupRelation="or">
      <DnsQuery onmatch="exclude">
        <QueryName name="exclude=Microsoft DNS query" condition="end with">.microsoft.com</QueryName>
        <QueryName name="exclude=Windows Update DNS query" condition="end with">.windowsupdate.com</QueryName>
        <QueryName name="exclude=Windows DNS query" condition="end with">.windows.com</QueryName>
      </DnsQuery>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 23: FILE DELETE (ARCHIVED) [FileDelete]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="FileDelete" groupRelation="or">
      <FileDelete onmatch="include"/>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 25: PROCESS TAMPERING [ProcessTampering]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="ProcessTampering" groupRelation="or">
      <ProcessTampering onmatch="exclude"/>
    </RuleGroup>

    <!--
    ================================================================
    EVENT ID 26: FILE DELETE DETECTED [FileDeleteDetected]
    ================================================================
    -->
    <RuleGroup name="FileDeleteDetected" groupRelation="or">
      <FileDeleteDetected onmatch="include">
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1070.004,technique=File Deletion,detection=Executable file deleted" condition="end with">.exe</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1070.004,technique=File Deletion,detection=DLL file deleted" condition="end with">.dll</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1070.004,technique=File Deletion,detection=System driver deleted" condition="end with">.sys</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1070.004,technique=File Deletion,detection=PowerShell script deleted" condition="end with">.ps1</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1070.004,technique=File Deletion,detection=Batch script deleted" condition="end with">.bat</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1070.004,technique=File Deletion,detection=Command script deleted" condition="end with">.cmd</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1490|T1485,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Backup file (.bak) deletion" condition="end with">.bak</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1490|T1485,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Virtual hard disk (.vhd) deletion" condition="end with">.vhd</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1490|T1485,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=Virtual hard disk (.vhdx) deletion" condition="end with">.vhdx</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1490|T1485,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=SQL Server data file (.mdf) deletion" condition="end with">.mdf</TargetFilename>
        <TargetFilename name="technique_id=T1490|T1485,technique=Inhibit System Recovery,detection=SQL Server log file (.ldf) deletion" condition="end with">.ldf</TargetFilename>
      </FileDeleteDetected>
    </RuleGroup>

  </EventFiltering>
</Sysmon>
